@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.dev/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

# A single, narrowly-scoped SHACL shape enacting the one hard constraint
# `vocabulary.ttl`'s bl:Epic class establishes: an Epic must never itself be
# a sub-issue of anything. See MODELING_NOTES.md "Epic modeling" for why
# this exists and what it deliberately does NOT constrain (an Epic is not
# required to have any children).
#
# This is NOT the full shape library #285 ("SHACL shapes validating backlog
# structural invariants") is scoped to build -- that issue's job is the
# fuller validation suite (labels, closed-issue consistency, crate coverage,
# etc). This one shape is narrow enough, and load-bearing enough for the
# ontology itself, to enact immediately rather than leave implicit.

bl:EpicHasNoParentShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass bl:Epic ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path bl:subIssueOf ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "An Epic (bl:Epic) must not itself be a sub-issue of anything (bl:subIssueOf must be absent)." ;
    ] .
